      "id": "q-1777116661614-dkt3j",
      "question": "Inability to produce semen in a man is called:",
      "type": "mcq",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "Aspermia",
          "isCorrect": true,
          "index": 0,
          "imageUrl": ""
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "Azoospermia",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "index": 1,
          "imageUrl": ""
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "Asthenospermia",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "index": 2,
          "imageUrl": ""
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "Tetrazoospermia",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "index": 3,
          "imageUrl": ""
        }
      ],
      "answer": "",
      "alternateAnswers": [],
      "explanation": "Aspermia: This refers to the complete absence of semen production, which may be due to blockages, hormonal issues, or nerve damage. It is often associated with ejaculatory dysfunction and can\nimpact fertility.\nAzoospermia: This condition involves the absence of sperm in the semen despite normal semen production. It is commonly caused by blockages, testicular failure, or hormonal imbalances, making\nnatural conception difficult.\nAsthenospermia: This refers to reduced sperm motility, where sperm are present but lack the ability to swim efficiently toward the egg. Causes include infections, genetic factors, or lifestyle issues like\nsmoking.\nTetrazoospermia: This condition refers to abnormalities in the shape and structure of sperm (morphology). Poorly formed sperm often struggle to fertilize an egg, leading to potential fertility challenges.",
      "hint": "",
      "marks": 1,
      "negativeMark": 0,
      "negativeMarking": false,
      "imageUrl": "",
